title: Veeam: CDP Jobs
agents: windows
catalog: os/storage
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors the state of the Continuous Data Protection (CDP)
 policies of Veeam Backup & Replication, the result of their last run and
 the time of their next run. If the policy is not disabled, the check also
 monitors the time since the last CDP sync. This is the time of the oldest
 of the latest restore points of all replicas of the policy, since the
 replica lagging behind the most determines the achieved RPO.

 In order to carry out the check, the Veeam agent plugin
 needs to be installed on the backup server. See special instructions in the
 comment section of the two Veeam agent plug-in scripts on how to install
 the scripts.

 - The policy state is {OK} if it is {InitialSync}, {Running} or {Disabled},
   {CRIT} if it is {Failed} or {Stopped} and {UNKNOWN} otherwise.

 - The result of the last run is {OK} if it is {Success}, {WARN} if it is
   {Warning}, {CRIT} if it is {Failed} and {UNKNOWN} for any other value.
   For disabled policies, it is only shown in the details and always {OK}.

 - The time since the last CDP sync goes {WARN} if it lies in the future.

 You can also configure upper thresholds for the time since the last CDP sync.
 The defaults are {WARN}: 1 day 6 hours and {CRIT}: 2 days.

 Older versions of the agent plugin do not send the result of the last run
 and the time of the last CDP sync. In this case, only the policy state and
 the time of the next run are shown.

discovery:
 One service is created for each CDP job created by the Veeam tool, including
 disabled ones. To leave out disabled jobs, disable this in the rule "Veeam: CDP
 job discovery".

item:
 The name of the CDP job.
